# GOLF/2 prelude — list runtime, higher-order ops, printing.
# Authored in code-page mnemonic form (\exec = the indirect-call op, byte 0x8D).
# It is encoded to raw bytes and prepended to programs by tools/golfc.
#
# A list is a heap block [ len, e0, e1, ... ] of **64-bit cells** (M4/W4A; they
# were 4 bytes through W3, which truncated every negative or >= 2^32 element).
# A list VALUE is its address TAGGED in the top 16 bits — addr | 0x7FFF<<48
# (M-TAG2, W9-2A, moved from bit 48 / addr | 2^48 by W11-1A) — so
# `v >> 48 == 32767` is exactly "is a list" (see T).  Every word below that takes
# a list masks the tag off on entry with `16\shl16>` ((v<<16)>>16, idempotent,
# so a raw untagged block from A is accepted too) and every word that returns a
# list tags it on exit with `32767 48\shl|` (a shift, not the literal: the seed
# truncates literals >= 2^31 and selfcheck compiles this file with it).  A list
# of lists therefore holds tagged inner lists.  Header and elements alike are read with \fetch
# and written with \store, so element i of `l` lives at l + 8 + 8*i and A hands
# out cells*8 bytes.  Reserved runtime memory — ../REGISTRY.md §3 is
# authoritative:
#   0x4F0000             heap bump pointer — a byte OFFSET from the heap base
#                        (the address word H pushes; BSS-zero at start)
#   0x4F0010..0x4F002C   RETIRED — the old 4-byte scratch bank, now free
#   0x4F0030             spill-stack pointer (a byte OFFSET; BSS-zero at start)
#   0x4F0034 / 0x4F0038  heap base / span cells (A's state; T no longer reads them)
#   0x4F003C             retired code-arena bump pointer (unused since W12-O2)
#   0x4F0040             the entry rsp (argc/argv; ‹args› reads it)
#   0x4F0050             the stdin buffer block's raw address (W9-4C input)
#   0x4F0048, 0x4F0058   free scratch
#   0x4F0060..0x4F0098   scratch s0..s7 — stride EIGHT, all eight in use:
#                        s0 list · s1 index · s2 accumulator · s3 fn addr ·
#                        s4 result · s5 alloc temp · s6 filter count · s7 zip l2
#                        (W12-P3: € ⇤ ⌿ ⊞ use s0 as the element pointer, s1
#                        as its end and s4 / s7 as deltas to the result and
#                        to zip's l2 — see the W12-P3 section at the end)
#                        5177440 5177448 5177456 5177464 5177472 5177480
#                        5177488 5177496
#   0x4F00A0..0x4F00B8   lib/tio.golfj state
#   0x4F00C0..0x4F00F8   free-list heads, one per size class (A and ⌫, W9-3C)
#   0x4F0900..0x4F0CFF   W11 runtime cells, one 64-byte slot per W11 task
#                        (REGISTRY.md §3.1; the spill stack is at 0x440000
#                        since W10-C, and 0x430000.. is W11-1C's out buffer)
#   ..0x600000           return stack, growing DOWN from the top of the BSS
#   0x600000+ (moving)   the BRK HEAP — W6/M-MEM: the list heap is whatever the
#                        kernel gives back, starting at the program break and
#                        ASLR-shifted, so its base is READ (0⌸) and never named
# Do not touch any of it from your program.
#
# The four cells at 0x4F0030..0x4F003C did NOT move and did NOT widen: they are
# forever pointer-valued (all < 2^31) — the heap-base cell was baked into the
# M-VEC templates until M-TAG2 dropped the range filter — and their 4-byte stride is what
# makes the plain `@`/`!` on them correct.  Widening the scratch bank in place
# was impossible for the same reason its cells were 4 apart — s0's 64-bit value
# would land on top of s1 — so W4A RELOCATED the bank to an 8-byte stride
# instead of moving anything that other code hard-codes.
#
# Re-entrancy.  Scratch is global, so a looping word cannot nest inside itself
# (map inside map would clobber s0/s1/s3/s4).  Every scratch-using looping word
# is therefore bracketed by X (push a callee-save frame: copy s0..s7 to the
# spill stack, bump the pointer) and Y (pop it back).  The word's result is
# lifted onto the data stack *before* Y, which is stack-neutral.  X and Y use no
# scratch themselves — only the data stack and absolute addresses — so they are
# trivially re-entrant.  This is what lets a mapped function call map/sum/range.
# s5 is A-only (and ⌫'s, the allocator's other leaf) and is never held across
# a call, so neither needs a frame of its own (X's save set covers it anyway).  I is scratch-free and stays unwrapped — it
# is the hot path.  Since W12-P3 so are ⍳ ∑ ∏ ⌽: they call no user function,
# keep their pointers on the data stack and their constants in slot P3's
# cells (REGISTRY §3.2), and nothing they call can reach them again.
#
# Totality.  `{…}` is a DO-while, so an unguarded loop body runs once even on an
# empty list.  Every looping word guards its loop with `<len> 0\eq [ {…} ]`
# (since W12-P3 the pointer-walking loops guard with `<p> <end> \eq [ {…} ]`):
# \eq yields -1 when len==0, so `[` (which runs on TOS==0) skips the loop, and 0
# when len!=0, so it runs.  Initialization that must survive the empty path —
# S's 0, P's 1, F's init, the length header of M/V/W/U/Z's freshly allocated
# result — stays outside the guard.  Z iterates over \rmin of the two lengths.
#
# Raw arithmetic.  All prelude-internal pointer, index and flag arithmetic uses
# the raw atoms \radd \rsub \rmul \rmin \rmax \rlt (0x91..0x96), never the bare
# ASCII + - * ⌈ ⌊: M-VEC makes those polymorphic (int/list dispatch) and the
# dispatcher would recurse through the prelude's own address math.  The raw
# atoms are the same machine code today and are guaranteed never-polymorphic.
# Two deliberate exceptions stay bare because they combine USER data and are
# exactly where polymorphism is wanted later: S's accumulator `+` and P's
# accumulator `*`.  (F/M/W/Z apply the user's fn via \exec — no arithmetic of
# their own.)
#
# The prelude must NEVER use \set / \get (→x / ←x).  The variable bank at
# 0x4E0000 is user space — one global cell per name — so a prelude word that
# stored to →i would silently clobber a user's i.  Prelude state goes in the
# fixed scratch cells above.
#
# Words (single-byte names).  In use: H X Y A L I R S N E M F Q P V W O U J Z.
# Reserved by ../REGISTRY.md §2 for wave 2: T D K G.  Free: B and C — that is
# the entire remaining uppercase pool.
#   H  -> addr             address of the heap pointer
#   X  ->                  push a scratch spill frame (callee-save s0..s7)
#   Y  ->                  pop a scratch spill frame
#   A  cells -> addr       allocate cells*8 bytes (free list first, then bump)
#   ⌫  list ->             free: give a list / A block back to A (W9-3C)
#   L  list -> n           length
#   I  list i -> x         index
#   R  n -> list           range [0..n-1]
#   S  list -> n           sum
#   N  n ->                print signed decimal ('-' then the magnitude)
#   E  ->                  print newline
#   M  list fn -> list     map (fn is a word address, via \ref)
#   F  list init fn -> x   fold
#   Q  list ->             print a list, space-separated (each elem then ' ')
#                          — recursive since W9-3B: an inner list prints as [a b]
#   P  list -> n           product
#   V  list -> list        reverse
#   W  list pred -> list   filter (keep where pred == 0)
#   O  str ->              puts: print a “…“ byte block
#   U  str -> list         chars: byte block -> list of char codes
#   J  list ->             join: print a code list as text (cell -> byte)
#   Z  l1 l2 fn -> list    zip elementwise over min(len l1, len l2)
:H5177344;                                          # H: heap-pointer address
# ‹throw›  msg ->   the runtime's ONE error exit (W11-0), catchable since
# W11-3A.  msg is a CODE LIST (tagged or a raw A block), the shape “text“U
# builds.  Every runtime error the prelude raises comes here (I's index, ∘'s
# arena, ⌫'s two guards, ‹get›, use after free, the file words) and, since
# W11-3A, X's spill-stack overflow too (through ‹_3a_spill›, which builds the
# message after unwinding).
#   * A handler is armed (the chain head 0x4F0B00 = 5180160 is non-zero, see
#     ‹catch› in the W11-3A section): the message, tagged, goes in 5180168,
#     ‹_3a_pop› unlinks the newest handler record and resets the spill-stack
#     offset to it, Y restores the scratch ‹catch›'s caller had, and ⊶ puts
#     rsp and rbp back where ‹catch› captured them with ⊷.  Then
#     `5180168\fetch^` pushes the message onto that restored data stack and
#     the epilogue returns through the restored [rbp] — ‹catch›'s own return
#     address — so ‹catch› returns to its caller with the message instead of
#     0.  No flush: output already buffered stays buffered and comes out
#     later, in order.
#   * No handler: exactly the W11-0 stub — ‹flush› (output the program
#     buffered reaches fd 1 before `GOLF:` reaches fd 2), `GOLF: <msg>` and a
#     newline to fd 2 (one write for the prefix, one per message byte), exit 1.
#     It parks the message in s0 and the index / staged byte in s1 / s2 —
#     harmless only because that path never returns.
# A leaf on both paths: it calls no X-framed word (and not I, whose failure
# path calls it); ‹_3a_pop›, Y (a forward call, data stack only) and ‹flush›
# are leaves.
# ‹_3a_pop›  h -> sp bp   W11-3A: unlink handler record h (an address in the
# spill stack: [h] sp · [h+8] bp · [h+16] previous head), make the record's
# own offset the spill-stack offset (so the record frame and every frame
# pushed after it are dropped, and ‹catch›'s scratch frame is on top), and
# push the saved stack pointers.  Leaf; defined ahead of ‹throw›.  h is held in
# the 3A cell 5180184 rather than juggled with the swap byte 0x5C, which
# `decode -m` cannot round-trip (see gtools/decode.golfj).
:‹_3a_pop›"5180184\store16\radd\fetch5180160\store5180184\fetch4456448\rsub5177392!5180184\fetch\fetch5180184\fetch8\radd\fetch;
:‹throw›16\shl16>5180160\fetch0\eq[32767 48\shl|5180168\store5180160\fetch‹_3a_pop›Y\spw5180168\fetch^]
 ‹flush›5177440\store
 “GOLF: “5177448\store 2 5177448\fetch4\radd 5177448\fetch@ 1\sys_
 0 5177448\store5177440\fetch\fetch0\eq[{5177440\fetch5177448\fetch8\rmul\radd8\radd\fetch5177456\store 2 5177456 1 1\sys_5177448\fetch1\radd5177448\store5177448\fetch5177440\fetch\fetch\rlt1\radd}]
 10 5177456\store 2 5177456 1 1\sys_
 1.;
# X/Y: callee-save spill of s0..s7 (64-byte frames at 0x440000, pointer at
# 0x4F0030 — still a 32-bit cell, still a byte offset, now stepped by 64).
# W10-C: the stack is 0x440000..0x47FFFF = 256 KB = 4096 frames (it was 28 at
# 0x4F0900), and X checks it: an offset of 262144 has no room for a frame, so it
# writes `GOLF: spill stack exhausted` to fd 2 and exits 1 (like ∘'s arena check)
# — one compare-and-branch on the hot path, and Y needs none.  This is the one
# prelude error NOT routed through ‹throw› when no handler is armed (W11-0):
# building its message with U would call X again and recurse on the full
# stack, so it stays inline (W11-1C: behind a ‹flush›, a leaf, so buffered
# output still comes out first).  W11-3A: with a ‹catch› armed (5180160
# non-zero) X first calls ‹_3a_spill› (W11-3A section), which unwinds the
# spill stack to that handler BEFORE it builds the message, so U's own X has
# room, and never returns here.  Data
# stack only: `&` (over) re-supplies the frame base for each store, `"` (dup) for
# each load, so neither word needs a temporary.  Every slot is a full 64-bit
# \fetch/\store, which is the whole point: a scratch cell may now hold -1.
:X5177392@"262144\rlt[5180160\fetch0\eq[‹_3a_spill›]‹flush›
 “GOLF: spill stack exhausted“5177440\store
 2 5177440\fetch4\radd 5177440\fetch@ 1\sys_
 10 5177448\store 2 5177448 1 1\sys_
 1.]
