# I: index(list,i).  W9-2B: CHECKED.  `&\fetch&\gt` is len >u i, so one unsigned
# compare rejects i >= len AND every negative i (which is huge unsigned); `[`
# then runs the failure path, which writes `GOLF: index out of range` to fd 2
# and exits 1 (through ‹throw› since W11-0) — before W9-2B `3⍳9⊇` quietly read
# whatever cell lay past the block.  The happy path costs over/fetch/over/
# compare/branch and still no scratch; only the failure path (U, ‹throw›)
# touches scratch, and it never returns.  The
# check is its own step in front of the untouched address arithmetic.
# W9-2A/M-TAG2: the list is masked ((v<<16)>>16) for the length read and again
# for the address arithmetic, so a tagged list and a raw A block both index.
# W11-2D: the length is clamped to 0 when negative (`"0\slt~$`) before the
# compare, so ⌫'s poison -559038737 (huge unsigned) fails it for every i; the
# cold path then asks ‹_2d_chk› first, so a freed list says `use after free`
# and only a live one `index out of range`.  Hot-path cost: five ops, which
# the prelude's own loops skip by calling ‹_2d_ix› below instead.
