#                  0x7FFF<<48 and among
#                  themselves by address — no structural ordering.
# Iterative bottom-up merge sort, O(n log n), one X/Y frame however long the
# list (no recursion, so the 28-frame spill stack is never at risk).  The input
# is copied by `0↓` into src; dst is a second block from A of the same size;
# each pass merges runs of width w from src into dst and the two swap; when w
# reaches n the sorted cells are in src.  s0 src · s7 dst (both raw) · s2 n ·
# s3 w · s1 i (left cursor) · s4 j (right cursor) · s5 mid · s6 hi.  The output
# slot is k = i + j - mid, so no 9th cell is needed.  A merge step is branch-
# free: both heads are read at CLAMPED indices min(i, mid-1) / min(j, hi-1) —
# always inside [lo, hi), so an exhausted run is never read past — and
