# --- W11 (round 3): one named section per prelude-owning task, in wave order.
# A task appends its words directly under its own marker line, never below the
# next one, so parallel branches touch disjoint lines.  2A 3B 4A 4D 4E add no
# prelude words; ‹throw› (W11-0) lives above, next to X, and 3A rewrites it in
# place. ---
# === W11-1A list tag 0x7FFF ===
# No new words: W11-1A retagged the list core in place (T, Q, ‹flatten›, every
# `32767 48\shl|` exit).  A list is addr | 0x7FFF<<48; see the header.

# === W11-1B Files ===
# File I/O for ordinary programs, on ⎈ (open=2 read=0 write=1 close=3).  Paths
# and file contents are CODE LISTS, the shape “x.txt“⊃ and ‹readall› make.
#   ‹open›      path -> fd         open for reading (O_RDONLY)
