# --- W3 hook installation (top-level init; must stay LAST) ---
# M-VEC — implicit vectorization.  The bare + - * ⌈ ⌊ now compile to a
# polymorphic template: it calls through a per-op HOOK CELL when that cell is
# non-zero, and runs the plain scalar op when it is zero (tools/mkblob2._poly).
# The cells are BSS, so installing the five dispatchers below is exactly what
# switches implicit vectorization ON — and why every compiler binary, which
# never runs this prelude, stays byte-for-byte scalar and keeps its fixpoint.
# Cell = 0x4F0100 + 8*op byte (REGISTRY.md §3, stride 8 because the call reads a
# full 64-bit cell):  '+' 0x2B -> 5177944 · '-' 0x2D -> 5177960 ·
# '*' 0x2A -> 5177936 · ⌈ max 0x88 -> 5178688 · ⌊ min 0x89 -> 5178696.
# Each hook is the address of the matching ∔ ∸ ⨰ ⩌ ⩍ word.  Since M-TAG2 the
# template's filter is EXACT — `cmp word [rsp+6],1` / `[rsp+14]`, the same high-
# word test as T — so only a real list operand reaches D; D still re-tests both
# operands and falls back to the raw scalar op, so the hooks would stay correct
# behind a looser filter too.  32-bit `!` is enough —
# BSS leaves each cell's high half zero.  Must stay last: ′ needs the words.
\ref\vadd 5177944!\ref\vsub 5177960!\ref\vmul 5177936!\ref\vmax 5178688!\ref\vmin 5178696!

# === W12-O1 atoms on lists ===
# ‹_12o1_nan›  v -> v   the not-a-number hook of the unary arithmetic atoms
# ± ⊕ ⊖ ² ⊗ ⊘ (cell 0x4F0DC0 = 5180864, tools/mkblob2.NAN_HOOK).  Their
# templates call it only when TOS's top byte is 0x7F, a loose superset of the
# tag; here the test is exact: v is a list iff it is tagged (T) AND its
# address lies in the list heap (addr - base <u span, A's own two cells, the
# test ⌫ makes).  Then `GOLF: not a number` through ‹throw›, so ‹catch› takes
# it.  Anything else — INT64_MAX, any int in the tag band that no heap could
# hold — returns untouched and the atom's scalar body runs on it as before.
# A leaf on the happy path: no scratch, stack-neutral.  The prelude's own
# uses of these atoms are all on ints (lengths, indices, flags), so none of
# them can reach the throw.  Installed LAST, after the W3 hooks, so no init
# code above it can trip the check.
:‹_12o1_nan›"T["16\shl16>5177396@\rsub5177400@\rlt1\radd[“not a number“U‹throw›]];
:‹_12o1_init›\ref‹_12o1_nan›5180864\store;
‹_12o1_init›

# === W12-Z4 store-at, vector, deque ===
# ⍈ (0xD5)  l i v -> l   l[i] = v IN PLACE, and l comes back unchanged (the
# same tagged value).  The twin of ⊇: the same one unsigned compare, so i >= ≢l
# and every negative i (no counting from the end, as with ⊇) is `index out of
# range` through ‹throw›.  As in ⊇, a negative length is clamped to 0 before
# the compare, so a freed list (whose length cell holds ⌫'s poison) always
# fails it, and the cold path asks ‹_2d_chk› first: `use after free`.  Every
# word here checks for a freed block that way, off the hot path: a pop or a
# peek tests n > 0 (signed), a push clamps a negative capacity (⌫ also
# writes -cap into the header) to 0, so it fails the room test and the
# growth path's ‹_2d_chk› throws.
#
# A VECTOR IS A LIST.  A's header cell (at payload-8) already holds the
# block's capacity in cells, the request rounded up to its size class, so
# every list has room for cap-1 elements and most have spare: 5⍳ asked for 6
# cells and got 8.  ⍆ (0xD6)  v x -> v'  writes x at element len and bumps the
# length cell when len+1 < cap; otherwise ‹_12z4_vgrow› gets a block of 2*cap
# cells (A's classes are powers of two times 4, so the doubled request is an
# exact class and nothing is wasted; past 256 cells class 7 gives exactly what
# is asked), copies the length cell and the elements, gives the OLD block to
# ⌫ and pushes into the new one.  So the result is the same v while there is
# room and a new v after a growth, and the caller must keep the returned
# value, as with Go's append: `←v x⍆→v`.  The old value is then a freed list
# (`use after free` on its next list word, until A reuses the block).  The
# length cell stays first, so every list word reads a vector; ⌫ of the
# current v frees the current block, and ‹heapstats› stays exact (a growth is
# one A and one ⌫: the block count is unchanged, the bytes grow).  ⍆ appends
# in place, so any other copy of v sees it (a list from ⍳ € … included).
# Amortized O(1): a growth copies len cells and doubles the room.
# ⍅ (0xD7)  v -> v x   x is the last element, removed (the length cell drops;
# the block never shrinks or moves, so v is unchanged).  Empty: `pop from
# empty`.  ‹last› / ‹first›  v -> x  peek; empty is ⊇'s `index out of range`.
# ‹vec› -> v  an empty vector (A(1): capacity 3, like 0⍳); ‹vecn› n -> v an
# empty one with room for n before its first growth.
#
# A DEQUE IS NOT A LIST.  It is one A block [n, h, ring of R = cap-2 slots]
# tagged 0x7FFD<<48 (the list tag is 0x7FFF, Q's nested marker 0x7FFE), so T
# calls it an int and the list words leave it alone, but every list word's
# entry mask strips any top 16 bits: ≢ reads n, the element count, and ⌫
# frees it.  Element k (0 = front) is in slot (h+k) mod R, at payload + 16 +
# 8*slot.  The mod is one compare and subtract, since h+k < 2R, written out
# in place wherever it is needed (a call cost ~15% on push/pop):
#     P j -> P j'    &8\rsub\fetch2\rsub&&\rlt[\rsub0]_     (R = cap-2)
# ⍆ ⍅ ‹first› ‹last› test the tag (`48>32765\rsub`, zero for a deque) and take
# the ring path for a deque; ‹pushf› / ‹popf› take only a deque (`not a
# deque` otherwise).  A full ring doubles (‹_12z4_dgrow›: the elements move to
# slots 0..n-1 of a 2*cap block, h = 0, the old block goes to ⌫), so both
# ends are amortized O(1) and ⍆ / ‹pushf› return the possibly-new d.
#
# None of these call user code, so they need no X/Y frame: the hot paths work
# on the data stack (with `&`, never the swap byte), what does not fit there
# lives in the Z4 runtime slot (REGISTRY §3.2), and A / ⌫ (s5 only) are
# leaves:
#   5180928 c0 the block (raw payload address)
#   5180936 c1 the value being stored, pushed or popped
#   5180944 c2 ⍈'s index · the new block in a growth
#   5180952 c3 n (⍆'s growth: len+1; ⍅ on a deque: the new count)
#   5180960 c4 a deque's head h
#   5180968 c5 … 5180984 c7 free
:\putat 5180936\store5180944\store"16\shl16>"5180928\store\fetch"0\slt~$5180944\fetch\gt[
 5180928\fetch‹_2d_chk›_“index out of range“U‹throw›]
 5180936\fetch5180928\fetch5180944\fetch8\rmul\radd8\radd\store;
# ‹_12z4_empty› / ‹_12z4_oor›  P n ->   the cold path of a pop / a peek whose
# count n is not > 0 (signed): a freed block's poison is negative, so these
# first ask ‹_2d_chk› (`use after free`), then throw `pop from empty` /
# `index out of range`.  The hot paths therefore only mask the tag and test
# n, as ⊇ does, instead of calling ‹_2d_chk› every time.
