# === W12-P3 tight list-word loops ===
# R S P V (above) call no user function, so they keep their end and element
# pointers on the data stack and their one or two constants in this task's
# cells (REGISTRY §3.2, slot P3): R the end 5180808 · S P the accumulator
# 5180816 · V the source base 5180808, the result 5180800 and the mirror
# constant 5180816.  Nothing they call reaches them again (S's + and P's *
# on lists go to the ‹_12p3_…› words below, which use s0..s7 under their own
# spill frame), so they take no spill frame.  M F W Z do call the user's
# function, so their loop state stays in s0..s7 under one X/Y per call (the
# function may re-enter them) and the caller's stack is directly under the
# element (the A1 contract); each now walks ONE pointer cell s0 against an end
# cell s1 and writes through a constant delta, instead of an index cell, a
# checked ‹_2d_ix› and a length re-read per element.
#
# The elementwise engine behind the vectorized + - * ⌊ ⌈ (∔ ∸ ⨰ ⩍ ⩌).  Before
# W12-P3 a list operand went ∔ -> D -> Z/K/G, and Z/K/G ⍎'d ∔ itself on every
# element pair: two spill frames per call and a full shape dispatch (two T
# calls) per element.  Now ∔'s list path is ‹_12p3_add› (and so on per op):
# ONE spill frame, the word itself in s3 for the recursion, and one of three
# loops by shape — ‹_12p3_ll…› (list,list over the shorter length, as Z),
# ‹_12p3_li…› (list,scalar, as K), ‹_12p3_il…› (scalar,list, as G), each
# set up by the shared ‹_12p3_ll› ‹_12p3_li› ‹_12p3_il› (the checks, the
# result's allocation and the cells below; they leave [end p]).  Each loop
# keeps its end and element pointer on the data stack (nothing here calls user
