# byte-for-byte the same as the prelude's own ′\max / ′\min thunk (every ′⌈
# makes a fresh thunk at its own address, but the bytes — prologue, M-VEC
# template, epilogue — are fixed and position independent; their length is
# the rel32 of the jmp in front of the prelude's thunk), is max / min.  A plain
# `:m⌈;` compiles to the same bytes, so it is recognised too.  For max / min
# on a list with no list elements (‹_12a5_ints›) ‹_12a5_mono› runs a
# monotonic deque: O(≢l) in all, whatever n.  The deque is an A block of ≢l
