# === W12-O2 freeable thunks ===
# ∘ and ⊸ (above, in M-CHAIN and W11-2C) now take their thunk from A, `5A`:
# five cells for 39 / 38 bytes of code, which A rounds to its 8-cell class, so
# a thunk costs 72 bytes with its header and ‹heapstats› counts it.  The
# thunk's address is the block's payload, UNTAGGED, so it is still an int to T
# and to every list word, and `⌫` takes it as a raw A block: it goes back on
# class 1's free list, and the double-free test (a negative header) and the
# non-heap test work on it as on any block.  The 1680-thunk lifetime cap is
# gone; so is `compose arena exhausted`.
#
# The heap holds code, so it must be executable.  brk memory is R+W only
# (x86-64 Linux sets READ_IMPLIES_EXEC only for 32-bit programs), so the
# prelude asks for it: mprotect(base & ~4095, span + (base & 4095),
# PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE|PROT_EXEC) through ⎈ (syscall 10), once at startup
# right after the first brk (the W6 allocator block) and again in A's growth
# path after each brk, over the whole [base, base+span).  That is two
# prelude lines and no compiler or template change: the alternative, a
# separate mmap(PROT_EXEC) arena with its own free list, would have needed a
# second allocator, a second ⌫ path and its own ‹heapstats›.  The price is
# that list memory is executable too (W^X is not kept; the load segment never
# kept it either).
#
# What a freed thunk does: ⌫ writes its poison -559038737 over the first 8
# bytes, so calling a freed thunk executes 0xEF (`out dx, eax`, privileged)
# and dies with SIGSEGV — loud, but not a `GOLF:` message, because ⍎ is a bare
# `call` with no check.  As with a list, a stale copy of a thunk whose block
# A has since handed out again is NOT caught.  The old arena 0x4D0000…0x4DFFFF
# and its bump pointer 0x4F003C are no longer used.  This task's runtime slot
# (5181376 … 5181432) is unused by O2; O3 below borrows two of its cells.

# === W12-O3 priority queue ===
# ‹pq›  -> q              an empty min-priority queue (an empty ‹vec›).
# ‹pqpush›  q x -> q'     insert x.  Like ⍆, keep the returned q': a growth
#                         moves the vector (the old value is then freed).
# ‹pqpop›  q -> q x       remove and return the smallest element; q itself
#                         never moves.  Empty: `pop from empty` via ‹throw›.
# ‹pqtop›  q -> x         peek at the smallest (‹first›; empty: `index out of
#                         range`).  The size is ≢, and ⌫ frees a queue.
# A queue IS a list: a binary min-heap in array order (q[0] the smallest,
# children of k at 2k+1, 2k+2), so ⍕ shows heap order, not sorted order.
# Elements are ints compared SIGNED, as ⍋ and ⍒ compare keys; no key
# function — pack one in: priority<<32|payload sorts by priority, then by
# payload, for any signed priority and a payload in [0, 2^32).  Ties come out
# in no particular order (a heap is not stable).
# ‹pqpush›: x into c7, ⍆ (it appends, growing the block as needed), then sift
# up from i = n-1: while i > 0 and q[p] > x (p = (i-1)>>1) move q[p] down to
# i; then q[i] = x.  The loop is branch-light: p is computed with an
# arithmetic shift, so i = 0 reads q[-1] (the length cell) harmlessly and the
# i > 0 flag masks it.
# ‹pqpop›: n = ≢q; n <= 0 (signed: a freed queue's poison is negative) goes to
# Z4's ‹_12z4_empty›, which says `use after free` or `pop from empty`.  The
# length cell becomes n' = n-1, the top is q[0], last = q[n'], and last sifts
# down from i = 0: c = the smaller child of i (2i+1, or 2i+2 when it exists
# and is smaller); while c < n' and q[c] < last move q[c] up to i; then
# q[i] = last.  The sift-down walks CELL ADDRESSES, not indices (a = &q[i],
# so &q[2i+1] = 2a - P), which halves its arithmetic; child reads are clamped
# to E = &q[n'] (\rmin), a cell inside the block (it held the old last), so a
# leaf never reads past the block.
# No user code is called, so no X/Y frame: the state lives in Z4's spare cells
# and the O2 slot (REGISTRY §3.2):
#   5180968 c5  P, the queue's payload address (tag masked)
#   5180976 c6  i (‹pqpush›) · a = &q[i] (‹pqpop›)
#   5180984 c7  x being pushed · last being sifted down
#   5181376 o0  E = &q[n'] (‹pqpop›)
#   5181384 o1  &q[c], the chosen child (‹pqpop›)
:‹pq›‹vec›;
:‹pqtop›‹first›;
