# === W12-O6 booleans for output ===
# ‹tf›  f -> list       “true“ as a code list when f is 0, “false“ otherwise:
#                       the zero-is-true convention of [ ∊ ‹has› ‹startswith›,
#                       so `…‹tf›⊐` prints LeetCode's true/false.  A `≡ ≺ ≻`
#                       result (-1 for true) prints “false“; flip it with 1+
#                       (-1 -> 0, 0 -> 1).  A fresh list each call (⌫ frees it).
:‹tf›[“true“U⋄“false“U];
